            <ArticleTitle>Acute pain management in dermatology: risk assessment and treatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>543-60; quiz 561-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jaad.2015.04.050</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0190-9622(15)01622-9</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Dermatologists perform many procedures that require acute pain control with local anesthesia and, in some cases, management of postoperative pain. Identifying early risk factors before a procedure can better prepare both the patient and provider anticipate acute postsurgical pain needs. Taking a multimodal, algorithmic approach to managing acute postsurgical pain in dermatology practice can effectively attenuate acute postsurgical paint and reduce patient opioid requirements.</AbstractText>
